      "description": "Watch Toronto FC vs Charlotte highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The MLS clash between Toronto FC and Charlotte delivered a masterclass in offensive football and dramatic twists that kept fans breathless until the final whistle. In a match defined by crucial officiating decisions and a flurry of goals, both sides fought relentlessly for every inch of the pitch. An Explosive Opening Half On August 20, 2026, the match ignited from the very first whistle. Charlotte wasted no time establishing dominance, as Rodolfo Aloko found the net in just the 8th minute following a brilliant setup by Ashley Westwood . The hosts responded almost instantly; by the 14th minute, Markus Cimermancic had restored parity for Toronto FC with an assist from Joshua Sargent . However, the see-saw nature of the contest continued when Idan Toklomati reclaimed the lead for the visitors in the 20th minute, capping off a frantic opening twenty minutes of pure entertainment. Red Card and a Ten-Man Defiance The second half took a dramatic turn in the 56th minute when Walker Zimmerman was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from the Charlotte players, who felt aggrieved by the dismissal. Despite the numerical disadvantage, the visitors pulled off the improbable just two minutes later. Henry Kessler rose to the occasion, converting another Ashley Westwood assist to extend the lead to 3-1. This left Toronto FC facing a daunting mountain to climb despite having an extra man on the field. Toronto’s Late Resurgence With time running out, Toronto FC threw everything forward to salvage the game. Their persistence paid off in the 77th minute when Daniel Salloi pulled one back after being played in by Theodor Corbeanu . The tension reached a breaking point as the match entered its final stages. In the 90th minute, the comeback was completed; Niklas Dorsch struck home following an assist from Derrick Etienne , ensuring the points were shared. After twelve minutes of stoppage time and a flurry of tactical substitutions, the referee finally ended a 3-3 thriller that will be remembered for its incredible emotional swings."
